{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 3b24ade6 and c479fcec for the cutover head (05d618e2).\n\n3b24ade6 Q1, canonical mode at scope creation. Choose (b). Scope\ncreation is the first site that 788bc90a names, so `core.ts:396`\npasses `canonical: true` for a new-format room. Replay and\nadmission then hold one rule.\n1. Spell `apps/counter/definition.json` canonically with Define's\n   `normalize`. Report the new Counter digest before you commit\n   the pin, as you did for the demo Site.\n2. Before that report, run canonical mode over every definition\n   file and every generated definition that a new-format room can\n   admit: Counter, Lending, the platform definitions and the\n   examples. Report every digest that changes in one list. I\n   confirm the list in one act.\n3. The test of head F that checks every pinned and generated\n   definition in canonical mode must cover each file in that\n   list. Say in the note why it did not cover Counter.\n4. The note lists each site that admits a definition into a\n   new-format room, with its file and line, and all of them pass\n   canonical mode.\n\n3b24ade6 Q2, the forged source fact. Choose (b). Compare the\nderived entry before you require the copy, where main compared\nfirst, so this case reads `mismatch` again. `mismatch` outranks\n`incomplete` when replay can establish both. If the comparison\nneeds the copy, or the change moves a ruled check, keep\n`incomplete` for that case and tell me which check.\n\nThe `#privateCopy` repair and the stronger verdict in the relabel\ntest are accepted. List both in the note.\n\nc479fcec, the store-format race. Choose (a). The code is main's,\nand this head does not change it.\n1. NF-5 (c288c917) gains one item: two processes that initialize\n   one new store must both succeed. Publish the format word whole,\n   by a temporary file and a link, so that no reader sees an\n   empty word. The rule that a partial word refuses then stays.\n   Measure on main first, and state whether the test fails there.\n2. If the cutover gate fails on that one test and on nothing\n   else, rerun the gate once and say so in the END act.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}